(1)
dug(t)dt=αg(t)−βgug(t) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d u_{g}(t)}{d t}=\alpha_{g}(t)-\beta_{g} u_{g}(t) \tag{1} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
(2)
dsg(t)dt=βgug(t)−γgsg(t) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d s_{g}(t)}{d t}=\beta_{g} u_{g}(t)-\gamma_{g} s_{g}(t) \tag{2} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
Furthermore, we assume that the gene and cell-specific transcriptional rate αg(t) is influence by the expression of Transcriptional Factors (TFs).

Suppose ug and sg are the abundance of unspliced and spliced RNA, and αg(t), βg, γg are the transcription rate, splicing rate and degradation rate, respectively. The dynamics of a velocity gene g is modeled as:
(4)
dug(t)dt=αg(t)−βgug(t) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d u_{g}(t)}{d t}=\alpha_{g}(t)-\beta_{g} u_{g}(t) \tag{4} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
(5)
dsg(t)dt=βgug(t)−γgsg(t) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d s_{g}(t)}{d t}=\beta_{g} u_{g}(t)-\gamma_{g} s_{g}(t) \tag{5} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
We assume that the gene and cell-specific transcriptional rate αg(t) is influence by the expression of Transcriptional Factors (TFs), while βg and γg are gene-specific constant parameters. Considering the wide usage of linear models for gene-relations in previous studies27,34-37, we model αg(t) as
(6)
αg(t)=ReLU(∑i∈TFS(g)wgi∗si(t)) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \alpha_{g}(t)=\operatorname{ReLU}\left(\sum_{i \in T F S(g)} w_{g i} * s_{i}(t)\right) \tag{6} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
In order to include more TFs in the modeling, we reserve those TFs that are not selected as velocity genes. These TFs are excluded from the velocity genes selection because their unspliced-spliced expression does not provide sufficient information, primarily due to high noise in the unspliced RNA. Consequently, we incorporate these TFs, whose spliced abundance is denoted as s′, into the TSvelo by directly modeling the process between transcriptional signal to mature RNA,
(7)
dsg′(t)dt=αg(t)−γgsg′(t) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d s_{g}^{\prime}(t)}{d t}=\alpha_{g}(t)-\gamma_{g} s_{g}^{\prime}(t) \tag{7} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
As a result, we can get the ODE model with parameters matrix A:
(8)
[dU/dtdS/dtdS′/dt]=A[USS′]=[−BWW′B−Γ00W′W′−Γ′][USS′] \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \left[\begin{array}{l} d U / d t \tag{8}\\ d S / d t \\ d S^{\prime} / d t \end{array}\right]=A\left[\begin{array}{l} U \\ S \\ S^{\prime} \end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{ccc} -B & W & W^{\prime} \\ B & -\Gamma & 0 \\ 0 & W^{\prime} & W^{\prime}-\Gamma^{\prime} \end{array}\right]\left[\begin{array}{l} U \\ S \\ S^{\prime} \end{array}\right]$$\end{document}
U = [u1, u2 …, uG]T ∈ RG, S = [s1, s2 …, sG]T ∈ RG, S′ = [sG+1, sG+2 …, sG+K]T ∈ RK, G is the number of velocity genes and K is the number of additional TFs which are not selected as velocity genes. B ∈ RG×G and Γ ∈ RG×G are the diagonal matrices consist of splicing rates [β1, β2 …, βG] and degradation rates [γ1, γ2 …, γG] for velocity genes, respectively. Γ′ ∈ RK×K is the diagonal matrices consist of degradation rates [γG+1, γG+2 …, γG+K] for these additional TFs. W ∈ RG×G and W′ ∈ RK×K denote the matrices representing the TF-target relationships for the TFs selected as velocity genes and those not selected as velocity genes, respectively. Using these gene-gene weight matrices, TSvelo can model the gene- and cell-specific transcriptional rate αg. The whole parameters matrix A ∈ R(2G+K)×(2G+K)

list-item.p:
Within-cluster velocity coherence (ICCoh). Within-cluster velocity coherence is initially introduced by VeloAE61, which measures the coherence of velocities within a single cluster using a cosine similarity score between cell velocities. We applied the function unitvelo.evaluate() provided by UniTVelo7 to directly compute the within-cluster velocity coherence. Using the same notation as defined above, the CBDir is calculated as follows:
(14)
ICCoh(c)=1|{c′∈CA∩N(c)}|∑c′∈CA∩N(c)vc⋅vc′|vc|⋅|vc′| \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \operatorname{ICCoh}(c)=\frac{1}{\left|\left\{c^{\prime} \in C_{A} \cap N(c)\right\}\right|} \sum_{c^{\prime} \in C_{A} \cap N(c)} \frac{\boldsymbol{v}_{c} \cdot \boldsymbol{v}_{c^{\prime}}}{\left|\boldsymbol{v}_{c}\right| \cdot\left|\boldsymbol{v}_{c^{\prime}}\right|} \tag{14} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
